[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3]

; ROOFTOP-1 (2026-09-05) - THE EIGHTH SECTION, AND THE SMALLEST THING IN IT.
;
; Talon, off the 2026-09-04 playtest, describing a route nobody designed:
;   "if you walk toward cyan that corner of the map and if you cross the bridge, and if you go to
;    the middle of the cyan map and turn left, and then if you jump off of that, you will be able
;    to stand on the top of the lab scene, which is fantastic. I love it please do not change this
;    ... and then walk across that little tunnel, and then if the player stacks golden cubes up if
;    they stack three of them, they would be able to jump up onto the top of that other area so I
;    would like to put something special up here that the player can get to."
; and, on the first siting of that something special:
;   "That's the wrong roof. It's the one farther back. It's the one out more."
;
; THERE ARE TWO ROOFS AND THE TELEVISION IS ON THE SECOND ONE. Measured off the shipped scenes:
;
;   the LANDING roof   Lab/HubAccess_Off/Ceiling   top y = -6.410   x  78.55..101.45  z 81.31..98.69
;   "that little tunnel"  Route/HallCeil           top y = -16.070  x 115.81..171.83  z 69.58..74.54
;   the FAR roof       Route/VoidCeil              top y = -12.206  x 162.04..173.90  z 74.13..85.45
;
; Centre to centre the two roofs are 78.64 m apart in plan (77.97 east, 10.21 north) and the far
; one is 5.796 m LOWER. The climb off the tunnel onto it is 3.864 m. THIS FILE AUTHORS ONE PAD ON
; THE FAR ROOF AND NOTHING ELSE - the landing roof, the tunnel and the cyan plate all belong to
; scenes this packet is forbidden to edit, which is exactly why "did the route change" is a
; question `git diff` can answer (tools/dev/rooftop1_route_probe.ps1).
;
; WHAT THIS SECTION IS. x 114..176, z 68..87, anchored at (145, 0, 77.5): the tunnel and the far
; roof, i.e. the last two surfaces of that route. It exists because a television needs a section -
; BubbleTestLayout.LabRoofAnchor carries the whole argument, and the failure message of the test
; that forced it is the reason rather than the rule: "a player on that pad is attributed to NO
; section, so the dwell log reports the opposite of the climb they just made."
;
; WHAT IS IN THIS FILE: one pad, 6 x 6 m, its top face 2 cm proud of the far roof, for the seventh
; television to stand on. Two centimetres and not zero because a coplanar pair z-fights and only a
; render shows it (.claude/rules/godot-scenes.md); two centimetres and not twenty because a player
; who has just made a 3.9 m climb should not then meet a lip.
;
; WHY THE PAD EXISTS AT ALL, given the roof is already there. PuffinLab.tscn is OPTIONAL - the
; level is required to come up without it (EGG-2 acceptance criterion 4, demonstrated by BUBBLE-1
; with the scene moved aside) - and BubbleTestSelfTest.CheckPropHeights rays down under every
; entrance television and fails one standing on nothing. A television whose ground is an optional
; scene is a television that falls out of the world in a build that is supposed to be supported.
; The pad ships in every build; the roof under it does not.
;
; ITS Y IS DERIVED AND RE-MEASURED. -12.336 below is the pad's CENTRE:
; BubbleTestLayout.LabRoofPadTopY (-12.186) minus half of the 0.30 m box. LabVoidRoofTopY
; (-12.206) is the one mirror in the layout contract of geometry it does not own, and
; BubbleTestSelfTest.CheckRooftopRoute rays the LIVE roof under this pad on every run and fails if
; the two ever stop agreeing by more than a centimetre. A mirror with an instrument on it is a
; mirror; one without is a second copy waiting to drift.
;
; NO NEW MATERIAL. neutral_gray.tres is shipped and role-neutral; materials are art-atmosphere's
; and this packet authors none.

[ext_resource type="Material" path="res://resources/materials/bubbletest/neutral_gray.tres" id="1_neutral"]

[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="BoxMesh_pad"]
size = Vector3(6, 0.3, 6)

[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="BoxShape3D_pad"]
size = Vector3(6, 0.3, 6)

[node name="LabRoof" type="Node3D"]

; Section-local. World = this + LabRoofAnchor (145, 0, 77.5), so the pad is centred on
; (168, -12.336, 80) and its top face is at -12.186 - which is RooftopTvPos.Y exactly.
[node name="TvPad" type="Node3D" parent="."]
position = Vector3(23, -12.336, 2.5)

[node name="Mesh" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="TvPad"]
material_override = ExtResource("1_neutral")
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_pad")

[node name="Body" type="StaticBody3D" parent="TvPad"]

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="TvPad/Body"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_pad")
